       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. A single 50 mg dose of amlodipine is in the range of a toxic ingestion. You haven't given a clinical reason, and I can't think of an indication for it in a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function. Doses above 10 mg daily add little blood pressure benefit and raise the risk of serious harm.\n\nI can do any of these:\n- **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum labeled dose.\n- **Enter 5 mg by mouth once daily**, the usual starting dose.\n- **Enter a different regimen.** If the goal is more blood pressure control, I can enter amlodipine 10 mg plus another agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide. You would choose the agent.\n\nIf you believe 50 mg is truly needed, please talk to the pharmacist or attending first and enter it through a pathway with dose-override verification. If you give me a different dose, I'll enter it right away."
